    turnFlow: "Players take turns playing one card. The played card may capture one card of equal value, or a set of table cards whose values sum to the played card's value. In Scopa Corse capturing is optional: a player may leave a card on the table even if it could capture. Clearing the table scores a scopa (1 point). After each round of plays, new cards are dealt. Play and scoring otherwise match basic Scopa.",
